# {{ fleet_name }}

{{ fleet_description }}

{{ fleet_name }} is a Fleet: a set of Mechs, each a knowledge base in its own
repository, with declared relationships between them. This repository is the
Fleet's Coordinator. It holds no records. It holds:

- **the Fleet's definition**, `fleet.yaml`: the [members](members.md), what one
  record of each is, and the [relationships](relationships.md) through which
  one member's records may link to another's;
- **the canon**, the files every member carries byte for byte, and the
  commit each member is pinned to ([the canon](canon.md));
- **the checks** that read every member together: that each member's own
  answers agree with `fleet.yaml`, that every member carries the canon at
  one shared pin, and that every link between records points at a record
  that exists.

[The Fleet model](model.md) is the schema `fleet.yaml` follows.

## A link between records

A record in one member links to a record in another with a
`CrossCorpusLink`, from the shared module `mech_shared`:

```yaml
habitats:
  - corpus: HabitatMech              # the target member's name
    identifier: ENVO:00002149        # the target record's id, verbatim
    relation: FOUND_IN               # one of the relationship's relations
    basis: LITERATURE                # one of its bases
    source_version: 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567   # the target's commit that was checked
```

Each member's schema has one link class per relationship it is the subject
of, made by mechmaker from the member's fleet answers, so the relation and
basis are checked in the member already. `just audit` here checks the rest:
that the target exists at that commit, and is still on the target's main.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `just qc` | This repository: lint, `fleet.yaml`, the canon, tests, docs |
| `just fetch` | Clone or refresh every member under `cache/members/` |
| `just audit` | The Fleet: answers, canon pins and links, for every member |
| `just status` | One row per member |
| `just answers <member>` | The member's Copier answers, from `fleet.yaml` |
| `just sync <member> <path>` | Copy the canon into a member's checkout (dry run; `--apply` writes) |
